12",1602.9],["2026-06-15",1659.5],["2026-06-16",1663.9],["2026-06-17",1668.9],["2026-06-18",1726.4],["2026-06-19",1721.6],["2026-06-22",1740.0],["2026-06-23",1709.7],["2026-06-24",1714.7],["2026-06-25",1671.0],["2026-06-29",1663.6],["2026-06-30",1630.2],["2026-07-01",1627.2],["2026-07-02",1687.4],["2026-07-03",1724.4],["2026-07-06",1771.3],["2026-07-07",1787.4],["2026-07-08",1727.9],["2026-07-09",1811.4],["2026-07-10",1854.6]],"qtr":"Q4FY26","ratios":[{"label":"ROE %","value":"21.5%"},{"label":"ROCE %","value":"22.0%"},{"label":"D/E","value":"0.1x"},{"label":"Int cover","value":"8.8x"},{"label":"Receivable d","value":"25.4"},{"label":"Inventory d","value":"60.9"},{"label":"Payable d","value":"6.2"},{"label":"OPM %","value":"11.3%"},{"label":"Promoter %","value":"59.3%"}],"s":"GRAVITA","sec":"Metals Recycling & Circular Economy / Lead, Copper & EV Battery Recycling","sec2":"Metals & Mining","sections":{"bull_bear":[{"body":"100% internally funded capex; working capital debt expected ₹700-900cr (metal-backed, hedged); no dividends or buybacks mentioned; focus on recycling verticals over shareholder returns","src":"concall","title":"Capital allocation"},{"body":"West Asia logistics disruption (10-12% of sales); MCX aluminum hedging delay (impacting Al growth); copper import supply chain risks; integration execution risk with RML; regulatory delays in EPR compliance; commodity price volatility","src":"concall","title":"Risks & watch-items"},{"body":"Confident, strategic, and execution-focused; emphasized disciplined capex, backward integration, and long-term CAGR targets; acknowledged near-term headwinds (West Asia, hedging) but framed them as temporary; tone bullish on copper and EV recycling as structural growth drivers","src":"concall","title":"Management quality / tone"},{"body":"Copper EBITDA/ton target of ₹65,000 implies >40% margin expansion from RML’s current ₹45,000 — driven by scrap sourcing synergy and value-added product mix, not just recycling; working capital debt is treated as ‘hedged metal inventory’ not traditional debt — a key accounting nuance; aluminum/plastic margins are intentionally suppressed until MCX hedging enables scale — a deliberate capital preservation strategy","src":"concall","title":"Non-obvious takeaways"},{"body":"- Capital allocation prioritizes reinvestment in capacity expansion and technology upgrades.\n- The deck does not provide specific details on dividend policy or balance sheet metrics.","src":"deck","title":"Capital allocation policy (investor deck)"}],"business":[{"body":"Lead: 48,889 tons sold (+7% YoY), EBITDA/ton ₹23,043; Copper: RML acquired (31,200 tons capacity), EBITDA/ton ₹45,000, targeting ₹60,000-65,000 post-backward integration; Lithium-ion: 6,000 tons/year pilot commissioned (Jan’26); Aluminum: EBITDA/ton ₹16,043 (sustainable target ₹14,000-15,000), growth delayed pending MCX hedging; Plastic: EBITDA/ton ₹12,328 (sustainable ₹10,000-12,000); Rubber: 30,000 tons/year capacity planned (H1FY27), EBITDA/ton ₹7,000-8,000","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"| Challenge | Beneficiary/Loser | Dir | Conviction | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| — | — | — | — | — |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers"},{"body":"- Gravita India is positioned as a leading recycling company with integrated operations across lead, aluminum, and plastics.\n- The company emphasizes its role in the circular economy, converting waste into valuable products.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Regulatory Compliance] The company underscores adherence to environmental and safety standards across all operations.\n- [Global Presence] Gravita has a diversified geographic presence with plants in India, Africa, and other regions, reducing dependency on a single market.","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"revenue: +10% YoY (FY26: ₹4,265cr); EBITDA/margin: +12% YoY, 10.6% margin (FY26); PAT (rptd): +21% YoY (₹378.8cr); PAT (normalized): +21% YoY (no major one-offs); order book: not disclosed; net debt: ₹118cr (pre-copper), expected to rise to ₹700-800cr post-copper capex and working capital build","src":"concall","title":"Financial scorecard"},{"body":"Lead: ₹19,000-20,000/ton sustainable (Q4 pressured by West Asia); Copper: ₹45,000/ton (RML), targeting ₹60,000-65,000 with recycling integration; Aluminum: ₹14,000-15,000/ton (current ₹16,043 due to price surge); Plastic: ₹10,000-12,000/ton; Rubber: ₹7,000-8,000/ton; Cost headwinds: elevated logistics from West Asia disruption, copper import costs","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"revenue growth: 20-25% CAGR volume through FY29; margin: copper EBITDA/ton to rise from ₹45k to ₹60-65k; order inflow: not specified; capex/commissioning: ₹1,700cr total through FY29 (₹700cr copper, ₹160cr Mandvi copper recycling, ₹14cr Li-ion pilot, ₹49cr Mundra lead expansion); commissioning: copper recycling (Mandvi) in 12 months, Li-ion scaling in FY27, lead expansion (Jaipur) in Q1FY27","src":"concall","title":"Guidance"},{"body":"not disclosed","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"Copper recycling (100,000 tons by FY29); Lithium-ion scaling; Rubber recycling (India + Romania); Steel recycling (long-term, post FY29); Value-added alloy expansion via RML","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["Q4FY26 concall summary","structured quarterly financials","investor presentation (23-06-2026)","Walk-the-Talk commitments ledger"],"thesis":"Gravita significantly expanded its footprint beyond lead with the RML acquisition and copper recycling capex, driving a structural shift toward higher-margin value-added copper and EV battery recycling; despite Q4 EBITDA pressure from West Asia logistics and aluminum/plastic hedging delays, the company is on track for 20-25% volume CAGR through FY29 with 20%+ ROCE expected from integrated copper operations.","tr